{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "# SR3 diffusion super-resolution on BioSR (Colab)\nWidefield (blurry, noisy) -> SIM (super-resolved) on real microtubule images from BioSR (Qiao et al., *Nature Methods* 2021; CC BY 4.0).\n\n**Before you start:** Runtime -> Change runtime type -> **T4 GPU**. Then run the cells top to bottom.\nCheckpoints are saved to your Google Drive, so if Colab disconnects you can resume from where you stopped."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Connect Google Drive and check the GPU"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "from google.colab import drive\ndrive.mount('/content/drive')\n!nvidia-smi --query-gpu=name,memory.total --format=csv"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Get the code\nIf `sr3_microscopy.zip` is in the top level of My Drive it is used automatically; otherwise you get an upload button."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# STEP 2: get the code (from Drive, or upload it from your computer if it isn't in Drive)\nimport os, glob, shutil, subprocess\nfrom google.colab import files\nos.chdir('/content')\nzips = sorted(glob.glob('/content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_microscopy*.zip'), key=os.path.getmtime)\nif zips:\n    z = zips[-1]\nelse:\n    print('No zip in My Drive - click \"Choose Files\" below and pick sr3_microscopy.zip from your computer')\n    z = '/content/' + list(files.upload())[0]\nprint('using', z)\nshutil.rmtree('/content/sr3_microscopy', ignore_errors=True)\nsubprocess.run(['unzip', '-oq', z, '-d', '/content'], check=True)\nif os.path.exists('/content/biosr_dataset'):   # dataset already downloaded in step 3 -> move it next to the code\n    shutil.move('/content/biosr_dataset', '/content/sr3_microscopy/biosr_dataset')\nos.chdir('/content/sr3_microscopy')\nprint('code OK:', os.path.exists('configs/biosr.json'), '| dataset in place:', os.path.exists('biosr_dataset'))\n!pip -q install tifffile scikit-image\n"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Download the dataset (~88k small TIFFs, about 6 GB; takes several minutes)\nMicrotubules only, already cut into 128x128 patches and split into training / validate / test.\nThe test set has 9 noise levels: level_01 is the noisiest (~15 photons), level_09 the cleanest (~600)."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "!git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/DeepTrackAI/biosr_dataset\n!for d in biosr_dataset/BioSR/Microtubules/*; do echo $d $(ls $d | wc -l); done"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. Look at a few pairs (widefield input | SIM target)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import tifffile, matplotlib.pyplot as plt, os\nroot = 'biosr_dataset/BioSR/Microtubules'\nnames = sorted(os.listdir(f'{root}/training_gt'))[:4]\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 4, figsize=(12, 6))\nfor i, n in enumerate(names):\n    ax[0, i].imshow(tifffile.imread(f'{root}/training_wf/{n}').squeeze(), cmap='gray'); ax[0, i].set_title('widefield (input)')\n    ax[1, i].imshow(tifffile.imread(f'{root}/training_gt/{n}').squeeze(), cmap='gray'); ax[1, i].set_title('SIM (target)')\nfor a in ax.flat: a.axis('off')\nplt.tight_layout()"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Settings for Colab\nA mid-size model (32 base channels, ~15M parameters) that fits a free T4. Checkpoints go to Drive.\nRaise `total_steps` if you have time; first check the it/s printed in step 6 to estimate how long it will take."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import json, os\nos.chdir('/content/sr3_microscopy')          # make sure we're in the code folder\ncfg = json.load(open('configs/biosr.json'))\ncfg['model']['base_channels'] = 32\ncfg['train'].update(out_dir='/content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr', total_steps=60000, batch_size=16,\n                    sample_every=2500, ckpt_every=2500, num_workers=2)\njson.dump(cfg, open('configs/biosr_colab.json', 'w'), indent=2)\nprint(json.dumps(cfg, indent=1))"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. Train\nLoading the 41k training pairs into memory takes a few minutes before the first log line.\n**If Colab disconnects:** rerun steps 1-3 and 5, then run the resume cell below instead of this one."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "!python train.py --config configs/biosr_colab.json"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# RESUME after a disconnect (run this instead of the cell above)\n!python train.py --config configs/biosr_colab.json --resume /content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr/last.pt"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 7. Watch progress: latest preview (rows: widefield | SR3 | SIM)"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import glob\nfrom IPython.display import Image, display\nlatest = sorted(glob.glob('/content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr/samples/*.png'))[-1]\nprint(latest); display(Image(latest, width=500))"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 8. Tune the sampler, then evaluate on the test set at several noise levels\n`Input` = the raw widefield image; `SR3` = the model. SR3 should win on PSNR/SSIM, most clearly at high noise."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "CK = '/content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr/last.pt'\n!python tune_schedule.py --ckpt $CK --steps 25 50 100 --beta_end 0.02 0.05 0.1 0.2 --n 32"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "BEST_STEPS, BEST_BETA_END = 50, 0.1   # <- copy the winner printed above\nT = 'biosr_dataset/BioSR/Microtubules'\nfor lvl in ['01', '05', '09']:\n    print(f'===== test noise level {lvl} =====')\n    !python evaluate.py --ckpt $CK --steps $BEST_STEPS --beta_end $BEST_BETA_END --n 150 \\\n        --hr_dir $T/test_gt --lr_dir $T/test_wf/level_$lvl --out /content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr/test_level_$lvl"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "for lvl in ['01', '05', '09']:\n    print('level', lvl); display(Image(f'/content/drive/MyDrive/sr3_runs/biosr/test_level_{lvl}/preview.png', width=450))"
  },
  
